(* Negative control nopin-noise: the session handshake over TLS 1.3 with the client that pins no certificate, against an
   attacker that holds the Noise identity key of the server (AUD-5, #389). The binding still stops a middlebox from
   relaying the handshake, so the attack that this variant must show is the one of the holder of the Noise key, which
   answers the client in a TLS session of its own: the pin is what stops it in tls443-noise-client. The queries that
   hold there must fail here. CI fails when they do not. *)

process
  ( Setup()
  | LeakNoiseServer()
  | Sessions(pin_off, bt_export, plabel_session, lab_exp_session, suite_hfs)
  )
